  "generated_text": "1. **Determine the number of sides of the polygon:**\n   The sum of the exterior angles of any polygon is always $360^\\circ$. If each exterior angle is $30^\\circ$, then the number of sides $n$ can be found by dividing the total sum by the measure of each exterior angle:\n   \\[\n   n = \\frac{360^\\circ}{30^\\circ} = 12\n   \\]\n   So, the polygon is a dodecagon (12-sided polygon).\n\n2. **Calculate the sum of the interior angles:**\n   The sum of the interior angles of a polygon with $n$ sides is given by the formula:\n   \\[\n   (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n   Substituting $n = 12$ into the formula:\n   \\[\n   (12-2) \\times 180^\\circ = 10 \\times 180^\\circ = 1800^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n3. **Conclusion:**\n   The sum of the measures of the interior angles of the polygon is $\\boxed{1800^\\circ}$.",
  "grade": {
